---
description: Build-system and cross-platform rules for CMake, Windows, Linux/Raspberry Pi, Android, and future iOS work.
globs: "**/CMakeLists.txt,**/*.cmake,cmake/**"
alwaysApply: false
---
- CMake is canonical. Generated IDE projects are never committed as authored source.
- Keep platform selection explicit with target-based CMake logic.
- Do not add global compiler flags when target-scoped options are possible.
- Do not hard-code local absolute paths.
- Dependencies must be pinned to known versions/tags before a milestone is considered stable.
- Windows-specific linker/compiler options belong behind `if(MSVC)` or equivalent target checks.
- Keep room for cross-compilation toolchain files under `cmake/toolchains/`.
